{
 "schema": "habait/printed-dims-map.v0",
 "about": "Where each printed dimension of the 846 sales sheet sits, in the plan.json frame (cm, origin = plan crop top-left, +y down). Stand-in for the dimension lines card 01's report.json will carry; plan_gate prefers report.json 'dimensions' when present.",
 "plan": "360walkaround/tours/apt846/plan.json",
 "intake": "Habait/studio/fixtures/apt846.intake.json",
 "how_read": "habait engine-builder (card 05), 2026-11-02, by eye on plan.json's OWN source crop Habait/tour360/apartments/apt846/_local/plan/plan-crop.png (3750x3900, 2.25 px/cm; read on a 0.4x overlay with the traced loops drawn, plan cm = px * 1.1111). NOT on Habait/engine/_local/apt846/plan-crop.png: that crop has a different origin and plan.json is not registered to it. anchor = the printed number's position (it sits on its dimension line); angle_deg = the line's direction (atan2(dy,dx), +y down); plan_gate snaps it to the room's nearest long edge within 12 deg and slides an anchor that falls in a wall perpendicular to the line into the room. Kind decided from the drawing before any chord was measured. Second pass (same day): the end ticks a_cm/b_cm of 342, 275, 744, 344, 160, 270 read on cm-gridded zooms of the same crop (label anchors sat up to 25 cm beside their lines); 348, 212, 210 keep the label anchor (ticks not legible at the zoom used). |a-b| vs the printed value is the reading check (344 reads 372: the bottom tick is misread, the line's position and direction are not).",
 "kinds": {
  "room_clear": "wall face to wall face of a traced room (or of an open-plan union): checked, 3 %",
  "overall": "outer dimension of the unit or terrace: needs the dimension line's end ticks (card 01), not checked here",
  "opening": "a facade opening length (the rescue opening): not a room, not checked here",
  "sub_element": "an element inside a room that plan.json does not trace (shower stall, closet niche): not checked",
  "partial": "a line that ends on a partition tip, not on a wall bounding the room chord: not checked"
 },
